import ObfuscatedEmail from "../components/ObfuscatedEmail.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy — Unpeeragogy" description="Data processing information notice pursuant to Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR).">
  <article class="prose max-w-3xl mx-auto prose-sm">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> 28 August 2026</p>

    <p>This notice describes how <strong>Fabrizio Terzi</strong> processes personal data of users who visit <strong>Unpeeragogy</strong> (<code>unpeeragogy.pyragogy.org</code>).</p>

    <hr />

    <h2>1. Data Controller</h2>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Controller:</strong> Fabrizio Terzi</li>
      <li><strong>Registered office:</strong> Bergamo (BG), Italy</li>
      <li><strong>VAT ID:</strong> IT04923300166</li>
      <li><strong>Contact email:</strong> <ObfuscatedEmail as="code" /></li>
    </ul>

    <hr />

    <h2>2. Data Collected and Purposes</h2>

    <p>This site collects only minimal technical data:</p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Consent cookie</strong> (<code>cc_cookie</code>): stores the user's cookie preference. Retained for 6 months. Legal basis: legal obligation (Art. 6.1(c) GDPR in conjunction with the ePrivacy Directive).</li>
      <li><strong>Theme preference</strong> (<code>theme</code>): stored in browser localStorage, never transmitted to the server.</li>
      <li><strong>Temporary server logs</strong>: IP address, user-agent, timestamp. Retained for a maximum of 14 days for security and diagnostic purposes. Legal basis: legitimate interest of the Controller (Art. 6.1(f) GDPR).</li>
    </ul>

    <p><strong>We do not collect</strong> profiling data, advertising tracking cookies, user personal data, or payment information.</p>

    <hr />

    <h2>3. Analytics</h2>

    <p>This site uses <strong>Plausible Analytics</strong>, self-hosted on <code>plausible.pyragogy.org</code>. Plausible is a privacy-first analytics tool:</p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>No cookies</strong> are set by the analytics script.</li>
      <li><strong>No personal data</strong> is collected or stored.</li>
      <li><strong>IP addresses are anonymized</strong> at the server level before any processing.</li>
      <li>Data is aggregated: page views, referrer domains, browser language, device type — <strong>not</strong> individual user behavior.</li>
      <li>The data is used exclusively to understand which patterns and sections are read most. No advertising, no data selling, no third-party sharing.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>For more details: <a href="https://plausible.io/data-policy" target="_blank">Plausible Data Policy</a>.</p>

    <hr />

    <h2>4. Third-Party Services</h2>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>GitHub Pages</strong>: this site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub Inc. may collect technical connection data in accordance with its own <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement" target="_blank">Privacy Statement</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Giscus</strong>: the comment system on Unpeeragogy pages uses GitHub Discussions. Comments are public and visible to everyone. Please refer to the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement" target="_blank">GitHub Privacy Statement</a> for how data associated with your GitHub account is processed.</li>
    </ul>

    <hr />

    <h2>5. Your Rights</h2>

    <p>Under Articles 15–22 of the GDPR, you may at any time exercise the following rights:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Request access to, rectification of, or erasure of your personal data.</li>
      <li>Request restriction of processing or object to processing based on legitimate interest.</li>
      <li>Lodge a complaint with the competent supervisory authority (<strong>Garante per la Protezione dei Dati Personali</strong> — <a href="https://www.garanteprivacy.it">garanteprivacy.it</a>).</li>
    </ul>

    <p>To exercise your rights: <ObfuscatedEmail as="code" /></p>

    <hr />

    <h2>6. Content License</h2>

    <p>All content on Unpeeragogy is released under the <a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/" target="_blank">CC Zero 1.0 Universal (Public Domain Dedication)</a>. You may copy, modify, distribute, and reuse the material for any purpose, including commercial use, without asking permission.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>